1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,720
Take Stripe payments with a WordPress
form.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:06,980
Easy Form Builder's Stripe add-on
runs on the Free Plus plan, no Pro

3
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:08,320
license needed.

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:11,840
Open Add-ons and install the Stripe
Payment Add-on.

5
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:16,847
Next, go to Panel, Settings,
Payments, paste your Public Key and

6
00:00:16,927 --> 00:00:20,360
Secret Key, and click Save.

7
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:23,000
Under Create, pick Payment Form.

8
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:28,980
Add Name, Email, and a Payment Single
Choose field with your prices.

9
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:34,880
Then add the Stripe field, and click
Save to get the shortcode.

10
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:37,120
Put the shortcode on any page.

11
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:42,540
Visitors choose an option, enter
their card, and click Pay Now.

12
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:48,053
Each payment is verified with Stripe
on your server and shows as Completed

13
00:00:48,133 --> 00:00:49,700
under Stripe Payments.

14
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:54,700
Get Easy Form Builder free on
WordPress.org.
